      "writtenOn": "2023-07-06T18:29:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apologies - missed this. It sounds like an extra soong_zip action for every Javac action?\n\nAs a sanity check, the presubmits on this change indicate that we are doing ~6500 soong_zip actions and prior to this change, we were doin about 2000 per typical build.\n\nThe median remote exec time of soong_zip seems to be about 1-2s, so its not going to be occupying the pool.\n\nAlso, I think these actions have a high cache hit rate? If so, I wouldn\u0027t be worried about this load increase on the java16 pool. I would give a heads up to bili@ / abdelaal@  before merging this change so they can watch out for issues.",
      "parentUuid": "3feaf524_ee580b85",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
